---
import Demo from '../../layouts/Demo.astro';
---

<Demo slug="zeck-residual">
  <div class="stage panel" data-stage>
    <p class="stage__loading" data-status>Loading the WebAssembly module…</p>

    <div class="stage__body" data-body hidden>
      <div class="controls">
        <div class="controls__row">
          <label class="field field--grow">
            <span class="label">Input</span>
            <textarea data-text rows="2" spellcheck="false">The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.</textarea>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="controls__row">
          <fieldset class="seg">
            <legend class="label">Overlay</legend>
            <div class="seg__group" role="group" aria-label="Reference inputs">
              <button type="button" data-overlay="none" aria-pressed="true">Just this input</button>
              <button type="button" data-overlay="canonical" aria-pressed="false">+ canonical Zeckendorf</button>
              <button type="button" data-overlay="all" aria-pressed="false">+ noise &amp; all-ones</button>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <label class="field field--narrow">
            <span class="label">Window (bits)</span>
            <input type="number" data-window min="8" max="4096" step="8" value="128" />
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="readout__cell readout__cell--hero">
          <p class="label">Residual · whole stream</p>
          <p class="readout__ratio num" data-residual>—</p>
          <p class="readout__sub" data-residual-note>—</p>
        </div>
        <div class="readout__cell">
          <p class="label">Bit count</p>
          <p class="readout__big num" data-bitcount>—</p>
        </div>
        <div class="readout__cell">
          <p class="label">Adjacent pairs</p>
          <p class="readout__big num" data-pairs>—</p>
        </div>
        <div class="readout__cell">
          <p class="label">One density</p>
          <p class="readout__big num" data-density>—</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="chart">
        <figcaption class="label">Residual by window size — mean with min/max envelope</figcaption>
        <div class="chart__frame" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Chart, scrollable">
          <canvas data-chart role="img" aria-label="Line chart of Zeckendorf residual against window size" aria-describedby="chart-alt"></canvas>
        </div>
        <p id="chart-alt" class="visually-hidden" data-chart-alt></p>
        <p class="chart__note">
          A canonical Zeckendorf word has no adjacent ones, so canonical form sits at exactly
          <strong>0.0</strong> at every scale. Structured text sits in the middle; random data at
          the ceiling. The spread between min and max at a given scale is the local heterogeneity.
        </p>
      </figure>

      <div class="lower">
        <figure class="hist">
          <figcaption class="label">Distribution of window residuals</figcaption>
          <div class="hist__frame" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Histogram, scrollable">
            <canvas data-hist role="img" aria-label="A histogram of residual values across all windows"></canvas>
          </div>
        </figure>

        <section class="scale-table">
          <p class="label">Per-scale detail</p>
          <div class="scale-table__scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Per-scale table, scrollable">
            <table data-table>
              <caption class="visually-hidden">Mean, minimum, maximum and deviation of the residual at each window size</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">window</th>
                  <th scope="col">mean</th>
                  <th scope="col">min</th>
                  <th scope="col">max</th>
                  <th scope="col">stddev</th>
                  <th scope="col">windows</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody data-tbody></tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="notes">
    <section class="note verified-note">
      <p>
        <strong>The definition.</strong> Residual is the density of adjacent 1-bits in a window:
        <code>adj11 / (n − 1)</code>. The Zeckendorf theorem says every positive integer has a
        unique representation as a sum of non-consecutive Fibonacci numbers, which in binary means a
        canonical word has <strong>no adjacent ones</strong> and therefore residual exactly zero.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="note claim-note">
      <p>
        <strong>What it is for.</strong> The repo frames this as a candidate tokenisation
        criterion: a continuous “surprisal” signal that could replace BPE’s frequency-based
        merging, since that signal is language-agnostic and needs no vocabulary. It is a
        measurement substrate for that idea, not a demonstration that it beats BPE — nothing here
        compares against BPE, and nothing claims it would.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="note retract-note">
      <p>
        <strong>Honest limits.</strong> A high residual can mean disorder, or it can simply mean
        a stream that is dense in ones — an all-ones stream has residual 1.0, which is a statement
        about density as much as about structure. That is why one-density is shown next to the
        residual, so you can tell the two apart.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Demo>

<script>
  import { invoke } from '../../lib/fib';
  import { debounce, need, needAll, setStatus, token, withAlpha } from '../../lib/ui';

  interface ProfileEntry {
    windowSize: number;
    mean: number;
    min: number;
    max: number;
    stddev: number;
    windows: number;
    means: number[];
  }

  interface ZeckOut {
    bitCount: number;
    residual: number;
    adjacencyPairs: number;
    profile: ProfileEntry[];
    histogram: number[];
    histogramMax: number;
    oneDensity: number;
    truncated: boolean;
  }

  type Overlay = 'none' | 'canonical' | 'all';

  /* References, computed here and sent as plain text so the Go side does the
     same UTF-8 conversion it would for any other input. */
  const CANONICAL =
    '1010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010' +
    '1010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010101010';

  const NOISE = (() => {
    let lcg = 12345 >>> 0;
    let s = '';
    for (let i = 0; i < 900; i++) {
      lcg = (Math.imul(lcg, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;
      s += String.fromCharCode(32 + (lcg >>> 24) % 95);
    }
    return s;
  })();

  const ALL_ONES = ''.repeat(0) + 'x'.repeat(300).replace(/x/g, 'ÿ');

  const status = need<HTMLElement>('[data-status]');
  const body = need<HTMLElement>('[data-body]');
  const textInput = need<HTMLTextAreaElement>('[data-text]');
  const windowInput = need<HTMLInputElement>('[data-window]');
  const chartCanvas = need<HTMLCanvasElement>('[data-chart]');
  const histCanvas = need<HTMLCanvasElement>('[data-hist]');
  const chartAlt = need<HTMLElement>('[data-chart-alt]');
  const tbody = need<HTMLTableSectionElement>('[data-tbody]');

  const out = {
    residual: need<HTMLElement>('[data-residual]'),
    note: need<HTMLElement>('[data-residual-note]'),
    bitCount: need<HTMLElement>('[data-bitcount]'),
    pairs: need<HTMLElement>('[data-pairs]'),
    density: need<HTMLElement>('[data-density]'),
  };

  let overlay: Overlay = 'none';
  let primary: ZeckOut | null = null;
  let refs: Array<{ label: string; profile: ProfileEntry[] }> = [];

  const LADDER = [8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096];

  async function boot(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      await invoke('fsvm.meta', {});
      body.hidden = false;
      status.hidden = true;
      await refresh();
      await refreshRefs();
      draw();
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    }
  }

  async function refresh(): Promise<void> {
    try {
      const { data: d } = await invoke<ZeckOut>('zeck.profile', {
        text: textInput.value,
        window: Number(windowInput.value) || 128,
        sizes: LADDER,
      });
      primary = d;
      out.residual.textContent = d.residual.toFixed(6);
      out.bitCount.textContent = d.bitCount.toLocaleString('en-US');
      out.pairs.textContent = d.adjacencyPairs.toLocaleString('en-US');
      out.density.textContent = d.oneDensity.toFixed(3);
      out.note.textContent =
        `${d.adjacencyPairs.toLocaleString('en-US')} adjacent pairs over ` +
        `${(d.bitCount - 1).toLocaleString('en-US')} gaps` +
        (d.truncated ? ' · truncated to the bit cap' : '');
      renderTable();
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus(status, (err as Error).message, 'error');
    }
  }

  async function refreshRefs(): Promise<void> {
    const wanted: Array<{ label: string; text: string; bits?: string }> =
      overlay === 'none'
        ? []
        : overlay === 'canonical'
          ? [{ label: 'canonical (no adjacent ones)', text: CANONICAL }]
          : [
              { label: 'canonical (no adjacent ones)', text: CANONICAL },
              { label: 'pseudo-random text', text: NOISE },
              { label: 'all-ones bytes', text: ALL_ONES },
            ];

    refs = [];
    for (const w of wanted) {
      try {
        const { data: d } = await invoke<ZeckOut>('zeck.profile', {
          text: w.text,
          window: Number(windowInput.value) || 128,
          sizes: LADDER,
        });
        refs.push({ label: w.label, profile: d.profile });
      } catch {
        // Skip a reference that fails rather than losing the others.
      }
    }
  }

  const refreshDebounced = debounce(() => void refresh(), 260);

  function renderTable(): void {
    if (!primary) return;
    tbody.replaceChildren(
      ...primary.profile.map((p) => {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        const vals: Array<[string, string]> = [
          [String(p.windowSize), 'num'],
          [p.mean.toFixed(4), 'num'],
          [p.min.toFixed(4), 'num'],
          [p.max.toFixed(4), 'num'],
          [p.stddev.toFixed(4), 'num'],
          [p.windows.toLocaleString('en-US'), 'num'],
        ];
        for (const [text, cls] of vals) {
          const td = document.createElement('td');
          td.textContent = text;
          td.className = cls;
          tr.append(td);
        }
        return tr;
      }),
    );
  }

  /* ---- Drawing ---- */
  function prep(cv: HTMLCanvasElement, w: number, h: number): CanvasRenderingContext2D {
    const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2.5);
    cv.width = Math.round(w * dpr);
    cv.height = Math.round(h * dpr);
    cv.style.width = `${w}px`;
    cv.style.height = `${h}px`;
    const g = cv.getContext('2d');
    if (!g) throw new Error('canvas 2d context unavailable');
    g.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    return g;
  }

  function seriesColor(i: number, primarySeries: boolean): string {
    const c = cssToken();
    if (primarySeries) return c.brass;
    const palette = [c.verify, c.retract, c.inkMute];
    return palette[i % palette.length];
  }

  let cachedCss: { brass: string; verify: string; retract: string; inkMute: string; rule: string; inkDim: string } | null = null;
  function cssToken() {
    if (cachedCss) return cachedCss;
    const s = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
    cachedCss = {
      brass: s.getPropertyValue('--brass').trim(),
      verify: s.getPropertyValue('--verify').trim(),
      retract: s.getPropertyValue('--retract').trim(),
      inkMute: s.getPropertyValue('--ink-mute').trim(),
      rule: s.getPropertyValue('--rule').trim(),
      inkDim: s.getPropertyValue('--ink-dim').trim(),
    };
    return cachedCss;
  }

  function draw(): void {
    drawChart();
    drawHist();
  }

  function drawChart(): void {
    const host = chartCanvas.parentElement;
    const w = Math.max((host?.clientWidth ?? 700), 300);
    const h = 300;
    const g = prep(chartCanvas, w, h);
    g.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);
    const c = cssToken();

    const all = primary ? [primary.profile] : [];
    for (const r of refs) all.push(r.profile);
    if (all.length === 0) return;

    // Log x: window sizes span 8 to 4096, five hundredfold.
    const pad = { l: 46, r: 14, t: 14, b: 40 };
    const plotW = w - pad.l - pad.r;
    const plotH = h - pad.t - pad.b;
    const sizes = [...new Set(all.flatMap((p) => p.map((e) => e.windowSize)))].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    const x0 = Math.log10(8);
    const x1 = Math.log10(4096);
    const sx = (v: number) =>
      pad.l + ((Math.log10(Math.max(v, 8)) - x0) / (x1 - x0)) * plotW;
    const sy = (v: number) => pad.t + plotH - v * plotH;

    g.strokeStyle = c.rule;
    g.lineWidth = 1;
    g.font = '10px ui-monospace, monospace';
    for (let v = 0; v <= 1.0001; v += 0.25) {
      const y = sy(v);
      g.beginPath();
      g.moveTo(pad.l, y);
      g.lineTo(w - pad.r, y);
      g.stroke();
      g.fillStyle = c.inkMute;
      g.textAlign = 'right';
      g.fillText(v.toFixed(2), pad.l - 6, y + 3);
    }
    g.textAlign = 'center';
    for (const s of sizes) {
      const x = sx(s);
      g.beginPath();
      g.moveTo(x, pad.t);
      g.lineTo(x, pad.t + plotH);
      g.stroke();
      g.fillStyle = c.inkMute;
      g.fillText(String(s), x, h - pad.b + 14);
    }

    g.textAlign = 'left';
    g.fillStyle = c.inkMute;
    g.fillText('window size (bits)', pad.l, h - 6);
    g.save();
    g.translate(11, pad.t + plotH / 2);
    g.rotate(-Math.PI / 2);
    g.textAlign = 'center';
    g.fillText('residual', 0, 0);
    g.restore();

    // Reference envelopes first, faint, so the primary series reads on top.
    refs.forEach((ref, ri) => {
      const colour = seriesColor(ri, false);
      g.fillStyle = withAlpha(colour, 0.1);
      g.beginPath();
      ref.profile.forEach((e, i) => {
        const x = sx(e.windowSize);
        if (i === 0) g.moveTo(x, sy(e.max));
        else g.lineTo(x, sy(e.max));
      });
      for (let i = ref.profile.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        const e = ref.profile[i];
        g.lineTo(sx(e.windowSize), sy(e.min));
      }
      g.closePath();
      g.fill();

      g.strokeStyle = colour;
      g.lineWidth = 1.5;
      g.setLineDash([4, 3]);
      g.beginPath();
      ref.profile.forEach((e, i) => {
        const x = sx(e.windowSize);
        if (i === 0) g.moveTo(x, sy(e.mean));
        else g.lineTo(x, sy(e.mean));
      });
      g.stroke();
      g.setLineDash([]);
    });

    // Primary: envelope filled, mean solid, points marked.
    if (primary) {
      g.fillStyle = withAlpha(c.brass, 0.16);
      g.beginPath();
      primary.profile.forEach((e, i) => {
        const x = sx(e.windowSize);
        if (i === 0) g.moveTo(x, sy(e.max));
        else g.lineTo(x, sy(e.max));
      });
      for (let i = primary.profile.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        const e = primary.profile[i];
        g.lineTo(sx(e.windowSize), sy(e.min));
      }
      g.closePath();
      g.fill();

      g.strokeStyle = c.brass;
      g.lineWidth = 2.5;
      g.beginPath();
      primary.profile.forEach((e, i) => {
        const x = sx(e.windowSize);
        if (i === 0) g.moveTo(x, sy(e.mean));
        else g.lineTo(x, sy(e.mean));
      });
      g.stroke();

      g.fillStyle = c.brass;
      for (const e of primary.profile) {
        g.beginPath();
        g.arc(sx(e.windowSize), sy(e.mean), 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        g.fill();
      }

      // Direct-label the canonical series where it sits: exactly zero, which
      // is the single most important fact on this chart.
      const canonical = refs.find((r) => r.label.startsWith('canonical'));
      if (canonical && canonical.profile.length) {
        const first = canonical.profile[0];
        g.fillStyle = c.verify;
        g.font = '10px ui-monospace, monospace';
        g.textAlign = 'left';
        g.fillText('canonical = 0.000 at every scale', sx(first.windowSize) + 8, sy(0) - 7);
      }
    }

    // Legend.
    let lx = pad.l + 6;
    const ly = pad.t + 10;
    g.font = '10px ui-monospace, monospace';
    g.textAlign = 'left';
    const entries: Array<[string, string, boolean]> = [
      ['your input', c.brass, false],
      ...refs.map((r, i) => [r.label, seriesColor(i, false), true] as [string, string, boolean]),
    ];
    for (const [label, colour, dashed] of entries) {
      g.strokeStyle = colour;
      g.lineWidth = 2;
      if (dashed) g.setLineDash([4, 3]);
      g.beginPath();
      g.moveTo(lx, ly - 3);
      g.lineTo(lx + 16, ly - 3);
      g.stroke();
      g.setLineDash([]);
      g.fillStyle = c.inkDim;
      g.fillText(label, lx + 21, ly);
      lx += g.measureText(label).width + 48;
      if (lx > w - 120) {
        lx = pad.l + 6;
        // Second row if the labels wrap.
        g.translate(0, 13);
      }
    }

    chartAlt.textContent =
      `Line chart of Zeckendorf residual against window size, log scale. ` +
      (primary
        ? `Your input: mean residual ${primary.residual.toFixed(4)} over ` +
          `${primary.bitCount} bits, rising to ${primary.profile.at(-1)?.mean.toFixed(4) ?? '?'} ` +
          `at window ${primary.profile.at(-1)?.windowSize ?? '?'}.`
        : '') +
      (refs.length ? ' Reference inputs are shown as dashed lines.' : '');
  }

  function drawHist(): void {
    const host = histCanvas.parentElement;
    const w = Math.max((host?.clientWidth ?? 320), 220);
    const h = 190;
    const g = prep(histCanvas, w, h);
    g.clearRect(0, 0, w, h);
    const c = cssToken();
    if (!primary) return;

    const hist = primary.histogram;
    const max = Math.max(primary.histogramMax, 1);
    const pad = { l: 30, b: 24, t: 10 };
    const plotW = w - pad.l - 10;
    const plotH = h - pad.b - pad.t;
    const barW = plotW / hist.length;

    g.strokeStyle = c.rule;
    g.font = '10px ui-monospace, monospace';
    for (let i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
      const y = pad.t + plotH - (i / 4) * plotH;
      g.beginPath();
      g.moveTo(pad.l, y);
      g.lineTo(w - 10, y);
      g.stroke();
      g.fillStyle = c.inkMute;
      g.textAlign = 'right';
      g.fillText(String(Math.round((i / 4) * max)), pad.l - 5, y + 3);
    }

    for (let i = 0; i < hist.length; i++) {
      const bh = (hist[i] / max) * plotH;
      const x = pad.l + i * barW;
      const y = pad.t + plotH - bh;
      g.fillStyle = withAlpha(c.brass, 0.8);
      g.fillRect(x + 0.5, y, Math.max(barW - 1, 1), bh);
    }

    g.fillStyle = c.inkMute;
    g.textAlign = 'left';
    g.fillText('0.0', pad.l, h - 8);
    g.textAlign = 'right';
    g.fillText('1.0', w - 10, h - 8);
    g.textAlign = 'center';
    g.fillText('residual', (pad.l + w) / 2, h - 8);
  }

  /* ---- Events ---- */
  for (const btn of needAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-overlay]')) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      overlay = btn.dataset.overlay as Overlay;
      for (const b of needAll('[data-overlay]')) b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b === btn));
      await refreshRefs();
      draw();
    });
  }

  textInput.addEventListener('input', () => {
    void refresh().then(draw);
    refreshDebounced();
  });
  windowInput.addEventListener('change', async () => {
    await refresh();
    await refreshRefs();
    draw();
  });

  let raf = 0;
  window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
    cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
    raf = requestAnimationFrame(draw);
  });

  // Re-read tokens on a colour-scheme flip, so the canvas follows the theme.
  matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').addEventListener('change', () => {
    cachedCss = null;
    draw();
  });

  void boot();
</script>

<style>
  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .stage {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem 1.6rem;
  }
  .stage__loading {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    padding: 2rem 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stage__loading[data-kind='error'] {
    color: var(--retract-lit);
    text-align: left;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }

  .controls__row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }
  .controls__row + .controls__row {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .seg__group {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .seg__group button {
    padding: 0.45rem 0.8rem;
    font-size: 0.83rem;
  }
  .field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .field--grow {
    flex: 1 1 22rem;
  }
  .field--narrow {
    flex: 0 0 9rem;
  }

  .readout {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 9.5rem), 1fr));
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .readout__cell {
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    box-shadow: var(--sunk-sm);
    padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
  }
  .readout__cell--hero {
    border-color: var(--brass-dim);
  }
  .readout__ratio {
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--brass);
  }
  .readout__big {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .readout__sub {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .chart {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .chart figcaption {
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
  }
  .chart__frame {
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    border: var(--rule-w) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    box-shadow: var(--sunk-sm);
    padding: 0.75rem;
  }
  .chart__note {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
  }

  .lower {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .lower {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .hist figcaption,
  .scale-table > .label {
    margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
    display: block;
  }
  .hist__frame {
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
